\section{The Dirichlet limit}\label{sec:dirichlet}

In the present section, we study the asymptotic behavior of the energy functional $E_\alpha$ as the parameter $\alpha\to+\infty$. In this regime, the functional converges to the classical Dirichlet energy, which we recall to be
$$E_\infty:=\inf\left\{\frac{1}{p}\int_\Om |\nabla u|^p\dx-\int_\Om fu\dx\ :\ u\in W^{1,p}_0(\Om)\right\},$$
achieved by a unique function $u_\infty\in W^{1,p}_0(\Om)$.  We are now ready to establish the   rate of convergence of $E_\alpha$ to $E_\infty$. 

