\section{Multi-Function Problem Generation Rules}\label{app:multi-problem-rules}

In addition to the three basic rules described in Section~\ref{multi-func-gen}, we introduce specific rules for each type of problem to better simulate real-world programming scenarios. For the bugfix type, we only allow the combination of single-function bugfix problems, since in practice programmers typically do not implement new code and debug at the same time.
For \textsc{CoreCodeBench}-\textit{Difficult},  we ensure that each problem contains at least one single-function development problem, and the total number of atomic problems $n$ satisfies $n\ge 3.$

