on DVS-CIFAR10
and N-Caltech101 dataset to verify that our proposed TRT method provides SNNs with more generalizability (Fig. \ref{fig:landscape}). On DVS-CIFAR10, the area of TRT's local minima is slightly larger than TET. Although the SDT method exhibits a larger minimum region area in the loss landscape compared to TRT, the contour lines of TRT are sparser compared to SDT and TET. This indicates that TRT is flatter than SDT and TET in both the local minima area and the global scale. On N-Caltech101, the area of TRT's local minima is significantly larger than TET and SDT. These results demonstrates that the TRT method exhibits smoother loss variations under parameter perturbations, indicating that TRT effectively improves the network generalization.

