\paragraph{N-Caltech101.} Fig. \sref{fig:ap_learning_curves_trt_ncaltech101}-\sref{fig:ap_learning_curves_sdt_ncaltech101} shows the learning curves of different methods on N-Caltech101 dataset. For TET (Fig. \sref{fig:ap_learning_curves_tet_ncaltech101}) and SDT (Fig. \sref{fig:ap_learning_curves_sdt_ncaltech101}), both of them exhibit identical trends in their learning curves: the training loss decreases gradually while the test loss starts to rise during the early stage, indicating  significant overfitting phenomena in these approaches. In contrast, the test loss of TRT maintains a persistent downward trend throughout training, demonstrating the effectiveness of TRT in mitigating overfitting.
% asfr
