\begin{abstract}

This paper revisits a model for the plasma frequency of a simple wire medium formed by a square lattice of parallel metallic wires. We provide a comparative analysis of existing formulae for estimating the plasma frequency and derive a new expression taking into account the second-order correction by the period to wavelength ratio. The proposed formula demonstrates superior accuracy for thin wires, with a relative error of less than $0.16\%$ for ratio of wires radii to period smaller than $0.13$, significantly outperforming previously known results in this range.

