% \textit{Existing Estimations.}
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
The plasma frequency of a wire medium is defined as a cut-off frequency for electromagnetic waves whose electric field is aligned with the wires (TM-polarized).
Throughout this article, we refer to the plasma frequency $\omega_p$ and the plasma wavenumber $k_p=\omega_p / c$, where $c$ is the speed of light in a vacuum. 
In Table \ref{tab:overview}, various equations and estimation formulae (approximations) for the plasma frequency of a square lattice of parallel metallic wires (rewritten using our notation proposed in Fig. \ref{fig:square_swm}) are presented.
