P-Tree is a goal-oriented clustering algorithm that maximizes the Sharpe ratio in the baseline specification. Therefore, we anticipate these test assets having economically large and statistically significant alphas against those ``inadequate" benchmark factor models.
With such distinct basis portfolios, we expect them to achieve higher mean-variance efficiency, spanning an efficient frontier that benchmark factor models fail to span. 
