\subsection*{Sky masking and survey geometry}
To minimize the impact of Galactic contamination and survey inhomogeneities, we employ two distinct sky masks in our analysis: a standard mask to exclude the Galactic plane and poorly observed regions (\autoref{fig:mask1}), and a conservative mask that removes additional areas affected by stellar contamination or photometric systematics (\autoref{fig:mask2}). These masks are designed to ensure uniform data quality, suppress spurious angular features, and enhance the reliability of our anisotropy measurements.

