    The second case is $d_0 > 1$. As in Case 2, apply the connected cover simplification process described in (a) of \autoref{def: simplification process}. The resulting augmented graph $\cG^s$ still satisfies $h^{-1}(1)=\{(0,\alpha) \}$. Therefore, we may apply the connected cover simplification process to $u^s$ to obtain a new map $u^{ss}$ modelled on an augmented graph $\cG^{ss}$. %As in the previous case, we may assume that no pair of markings $p_i$ on $C_0^s$ and $p_j'$ on $C_\alpha^s$ are mapped to the same point in $C^{ss}$. Therefore, 
