\section{Transversality}
\label{sec: transversality}


Let $\G$ be a connected $n$-pointed graph of genus $g$ as in \autoref{def: stable graph}. 
%Denote by $V = V(\G)$ and $E = E(\G)$ the sets of vertices and edges of $\G$. Note that the genus of $\G$ is 
\[
    g = \sum_{\alpha \in V} g_\alpha + h_1(\G),
\]
Note that by the Euler formula,
\[
    h_1(\G) = 1 - |V| + |E|.
\]

% \begin{definition}
